	affiliations = {National Institute of Technology Andhra Pradesh, Department of Electrical Engineering, Tadepalligudam, AP, India},
	abstract = {This paper proposes a new methodology for optimal coordination of network reconfiguration (NR) and Volt/VAR control (VVC) in the active distribution network by considering renewable energy sources, switched capacitor banks, and electric vehicle charging stations (EVCSs). NR and VVC are essential tools to enhance the performance of radial distribution systems by minimising active power losses and improving the system’s security and reliability. NR will decrease active power losses as there is a power flow diversion due to changes in network topology. Whereas VVC decreases active power losses due to power factor improvement. Because of the reliability considerations, NR is performed only a few times a day. However, the VVC is performed much more frequently. Coordinating these two controls over a day is essential for getting the best results compared to independent and sequential control. An integrated approach for solving the coordination of NR and VVC problems over a day is proposed. Total power loss and voltage deviation minimizations are considered as objective functions, and they are solved by using the Teaching Learning Based Optimisation algorithm. The simulation results are performed on IEEE 14 bus and IEEE 33 bus test systems by considering the wind, solar PV generators, and EVCSs. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.},
